From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Giuseppe Maggio <jertlok@proton.me>
Date: Sat, 8 Aug 2026 15:30:46 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] media: i2c: imx179: add Sony IMX179 sensor driver

Adds a V4L2 sensor driver for the Sony IMX179, used as the
front-facing camera on the Google Pixel 2 XL (taimen), where it sits
on CCI master 1 behind CSIPHY1/CSID1 and streams RAW10 through the
Easel MIPI bridge (see the easel-mipi driver).

The power sequence is load-bearing and comes from the vendor
devicetree, not guesswork: rails (VIO, then DVDD, then AVDD), then
MCLK at 24 MHz, then release reset, then a mandatory ~9 ms settle
before the first I2C transaction -- reading the chip ID any earlier
returns zeroes, indistinguishable from a dead sensor. MCLK1 is a
CAMSS_TOP branch clock, so the CCI device (which owns CAMSS_TOP) is
held awake across the sensor's power cycle; attaching the sensor to
the domain via power-domains alone is not sufficient, since the domain
only happens to be up at cold boot because CCI is already active.

Mode/register tables are decoded from the vendor's
libmmcamera_imx179.so and cover the sensor's binned, video and full
3280x2464 modes.

Signed-off-by: Giuseppe Maggio <jertlok@proton.me>
---
 drivers/media/i2c/Kconfig  |   13 +
 drivers/media/i2c/Makefile |    1 +
 drivers/media/i2c/imx179.c | 1217 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 3 files changed, 1231 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 drivers/media/i2c/imx179.c

